WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.160
- [Narrator] The House
Ways and Means Committee

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.310
voted along party lines
Tuesday to make six years

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.460
of former President Donald
Trump's tax returns public.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.440
- There being 24 ayes and 16 nos,

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.720
the motion to submit the
committee report to the House

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.610
is agreed to and the documents are ordered

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:15.990
reported to the House.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.610
- [Narrator] Trump didn't
voluntarily release

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.740
his tax returns and had fought in court

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.630
to block the Internal Revenue Service

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.160
from handing them over.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.410
The IRS hasn't completed
the Trumps' audits

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.003
for any of those years.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.540
Documents released by the Committee

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.230
show Donald Trump and Melania
Trump reported negative income

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:38.430
in four of the six years
from 2015 through 2020.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.490
For 2018 and 2019, the Trumps reported

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:45.030
adjusted gross income of 24.3 million

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.583
and 4.4 million respectively.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.700
All years combined, documents show

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.930
their adjusted gross income

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:56.930
was negative $53.2 million
during that period.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.420
The Trumps paid some form
of federal taxes every year,

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.860
but reported income tax
liability of $750 or less

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.693
in three of those six years.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.440
A spokesman for Trump on Tuesday night

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.177
called approving the release
of the tax returns a, quote,

00:01:13.177 --> 00:01:16.410
"unprecedented leak by
lame duck Democrats,"

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.510
and House Republicans said the action

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.250
sets a dangerous precedent.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.350
- After nearly a half a century,

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:27.350
the political enemies list
is back in Washington D.C.,

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:30.750
and we worry this will unleash a cycle

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.630
of political retribution in Congress.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.700
- [Narrator] Democrats
said that the full release

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.610
was necessary for public transparency.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.440
A full set of Trump's tax documents

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.280
was expected to become
public in the coming days.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:46.530
(dramatic tonal music)

